FOUND (s526w1, Data-Dumper t/dumper.t row 250 "names that are not simple strings": got `$(?^:) = [];`, expected `$bang = [];`).
Probe (scratch p-qrov3.pl):
  { package fish; use overload '""' => sub { "bang" }; sub new { bless qr// } }
  my $a = [4.5/1.5, fish->new()]; print "1 $a->[1]\n"; my $c = [@$a]; print "2 $c->[1]\n";
perl: "1 bang" / "2 bang".  PCL: "1 (?^:)" / "2 (?^:)".  `my $f = fish->new; "$f"` is "bang" in both (scratch p-qrov.pl).
Rows: Data-Dumper dumper.t 250 (+ its Dump twin if any).  Layer: runtime (the element read path of a blessed regex skips the overload table; cf. #2051).
